  "year": 2024,
  "arxivId": "2411.14199",
  "abstract": "OpenScholar is a retrieval-augmented language model that synthesizes scientific literature by identifying relevant passages from a large corpus of papers and generating citation-backed responses. It outperforms other models, including GPT-4, on a new benchmark called ScholarQA Bench, which evaluates the ability of models to understand and synthesize existing research.",
