    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "OpenScholar works by <strong>retrieving relevant passages</strong> from a large corpus of papers, <strong>generating an initial response</strong>, and then <strong>refining the response</strong> through iterative self-feedback and retrieval. This process allows OpenScholar to <strong>improve the quality and accuracy</strong> of its responses.",
